WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.440
Use the Integrated Scales of Development to connect listening with receptive language, expressive language, speech, cognition, and social communication.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:12.060
The age ranges describe typical development with considerable variation.

00:00:12.685 --> 00:00:15.645
Use them to choose goals and counsel families.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.940
One missed milestone does not establish a diagnosis.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:25.800
Sutherland demonstrates choosing an auditory-language reference range using listening experience.

00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:34.695
A child who receives consistent access at nine months has about nine months of that experience at eighteen months of chronological age.

00:00:35.565 --> 00:00:40.685
Keep both ages visible, and do not reset every part of development to the activation date.

00:00:41.575 --> 00:00:48.455
The lecture's speech-intelligibility percentages refer to understanding by parents, not every unfamiliar listener.

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:52.850
Some vocabulary values in the packet conflict and remain flagged.

00:00:53.590 --> 00:01:00.870
The practical goal is individualized monitoring, useful access to sound, and rich everyday interaction supported by family coaching.

